-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat deployer from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-seat-deployer: the seat questions of Articles 1 to 4, 111 and 113 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), asked by a deployer of an AI system: whoever uses an AI system under its authority, except in a personal non-professional activity (Article 3(4)).
--
-- LAYER 2 (the seat layer). Every question below calls a function of the keel (aia-scope, aia-definitions, aia-literacy, aia-timeline, aia-annex-x) and restates no rule.
-- The keel decides what the text means, the date it applies from and which text is in force; this file asks, in the words and with the facts of this seat, what a person in the seat can state.
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it. The role facts are asked once, in the question under Article 3 (or Article 2 for a product manufacturer and a person affected),
-- and no other question asks them again; where a keel function needs the role as a fact, this file passes TRUE.
--
-- THE DATE ASKED. Every question whose answer depends on a date asks `the date asked`. It selects the text in force (the Regulation as enacted until 26 July 2026, as amended from 27 July 2026,
-- the day the Omnibus enters into force) and whether the provision applies yet (Chapter I from 2 February 2025; the group General from 2 August 2026).
-- The other shared inputs (the placement date, the significant-change flag, the route by which the AI system is high-risk) carry the same name and @desc in every question that needs them.
--
-- RESULTS. A MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE DATE answer of NOTHING means "not covered": the provision does not speak to these facts, or has not begun to apply, or is not in the text in force on the date asked.
-- JUST FALSE is the text's own "no" (a flat negative such as "does not apply", or a condition it states). The answer of a keel function is passed through unchanged; nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- An exported obligation (a DEONTIC answer) is shown by a form as the placeholder "<obligation>"; its content is read with #TRACE in the case file.
--
-- STATUS. Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect (it says so itself, line 2 of the file).
-- The readings are the keel's (NOTES.md, fork register) and this layer's (NOTES.md, fork register P0): assumed, not ruled by a lawyer.
-- The Interact form and jl4-service were not run; l4 check, l4 run and l4 batch were.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`
-- Chapter I (Articles 1 to 4a) applies from 2 February 2025 (Art 113 third paragraph, point (a)).
-- Article 1 itself creates no rule (a purpose clause and a statement of contents): the one question a seat asks of it is whether the Chapter it opens applies.

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1660 | (a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025, with the exception of Article 5(1), first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb), and Article 5(1a) and (1b) which shall apply from 2 December 2026;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202 | Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;
@ref Art 113 first paragraph and third paragraph point (a): Chapter I (src:1656) (src:1660) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202)
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).
@export Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 1, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Article 2(1): does the Regulation apply to me?`
-- Article 2(1) lists whom the Regulation applies to; a seat asks the limb that names its role.
-- A party outside every limb is "not covered" (NOTHING): the list does not close.

-- src:34 | (b) deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located within the Union;
@ref Art 2(1)(b) (src:34)
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it, so the keel's role fact is passed as TRUE. Whether the definition of the role fits is asked once, in the question under Article 3.
@export Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my place of establishment or location` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you established or located in the Union, or in a third country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(1)(b), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in the Union` IS
    `Art 2(1)(b) the Regulation applies to the deployer in the Union` `the date asked` TRUE `my place of establishment or location`

-- src:35 | (c) providers and deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located in a third country, where the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union;
@ref Art 2(1)(c) (src:35)
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it, so the keel's role fact is passed as TRUE. Whether the definition of the role fits is asked once, in the question under Article 3.
@export Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my place of establishment or location` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you established or located in the Union, or in a third country?
      `the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the output produced by the AI system used in the Union?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(1)(c), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a deployer established or located in a third country because the output of my AI system is used in the Union` IS
    `Art 2(1)(c) the Regulation applies to the provider or deployer in a third country whose output is used in the Union` `the date asked` TRUE `my place of establishment or location` `the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union`


§ `Article 2(2): my high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (replaced by the Omnibus)`
-- Only if the AI system is high-risk under Article 6(1) and related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I.
-- The answer names, for one Article at a time, whether it applies to such a system.

-- src:41 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply. Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply. Article 57 applies only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
@ref Art 2(2) (src:41) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420)
-- The date asked selects the text: the list of Articles that apply is shorter as enacted (Articles 102 to 109) than as amended (Articles 102 to 112, and Article 60a).
-- The Article is asked as its number, the letter that may follow it (a for Article 60a) and a paragraph number (0 for the whole Article).
@export Under Article 2(2), as a deployer of an AI system, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the AI system is related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation?
      `the number of the Article I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which Article of the Regulation do you ask about? Give its number, for example 9 for Article 9.
      `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any` IS A STRING @desc If the Article has a letter after its number, give it, for example a for Article 60a. Otherwise leave this empty.
      `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article` IS A NUMBER @desc Which paragraph of that Article do you ask about? Give its number, or 0 if you mean the whole Article.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(2), as a deployer of an AI system, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products` IS
    `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the AI system is related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the provision I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the provision I ask about` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
            number IS `the number of the Article I ask about`
            letter IS `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any`
            paragraph IS `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article`


§ `Article 2(3): areas outside Union law, and military, defence and national security`
-- Only if the matter, the AI system or its output is in one of these areas.

-- src:43 | 3. This Regulation does not apply to areas outside the scope of Union law, and shall not, in any event, affect the competences of the Member States concerning national security, regardless of the type of entity entrusted by the Member States with carrying out tasks in relation to those competences.
@ref Art 2(3) first subparagraph (src:43)
-- The first subparagraph protects the competences of the Member States, "regardless of the type of entity entrusted by the Member States with carrying out tasks": the entity may be a provider or a deployer.
@export Under Article 2(3), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the matter is outside the scope of Union law or concerns the national security competences of the Member States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter an area outside the scope of Union law, or a competence of the Member States concerning national security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(3), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the matter outside the scope of Union law` IS
    `Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the matter outside the scope of Union law` `the date asked` `the matter is outside the scope of Union law or concerns the national security competences of the Member States`

-- src:44 | This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used with or without modification exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities.
@ref Art 2(3) second subparagraph (src:44)
-- "where and in so far": a system with a mixed purpose is outside the exclusion for the part that serves another purpose; answer yes only where all of it is military, defence or national security.
@export Under Article 2(3), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is placed on the market, put into service or used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system placed on the market, put into service or used, with or without modification, exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes? Answer no if it also serves any other purpose.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(3), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS
    `Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` `the date asked` `the AI system is placed on the market, put into service or used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes`

-- src:45 | This Regulation does not apply to AI systems which are not placed on the market or put into service in the Union, where the output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities.
@ref Art 2(3) third subparagraph (src:45)
@export Under Article 2(3), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is not placed on the market or put into service in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system not placed on the market or put into service in the Union?
      `its output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the output of the AI system used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(3), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS
    `Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the AI system not placed on the market in the Union whose output is used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` `the date asked` `the AI system is not placed on the market or put into service in the Union` `its output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes`


§ `Article 2(4): third-country public authorities and international organisations`
-- Only if you are a public authority in a third country or an international organisation that uses AI systems for law enforcement and judicial cooperation.

-- src:46 | 4. This Regulation applies neither to public authorities in a third country nor to international organisations falling within the scope of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1, where those authorities or organisations use AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States, provided that such a third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals.
@ref Art 2(4) (src:46)
-- The paragraph names the authority or organisation that "use[s] AI systems": the deployer seat is the one it addresses.
@export Under Article 2(4), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a public authority in a third country or an international organisation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `I am a public authority in a third country or an international organisation that falls within the scope of the Regulation under Article 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a public authority in a third country, or an international organisation, that falls within the scope of the Regulation under Article 2(1)?
      `I use AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States?
      `my third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your third country or international organisation provide adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of the fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(4), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as a public authority in a third country or an international organisation` IS
    `Art 2(4) the Regulation applies to the third-country public authority or international organisation` `the date asked` `I am a public authority in a third country or an international organisation that falls within the scope of the Regulation under Article 2(1)` `I use AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States` `my third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals`


§ `Article 2(5): the liability of providers of intermediary services`
-- Only if you also provide an intermediary service within Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 and ask about its liability rules.

-- src:47 | 5. This Regulation shall not affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services as set out in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.
@ref Art 2(5) (src:47)
@export Under Article 2(5), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the provision is a provision on the liability of providers of intermediary services in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision you ask about one of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(5), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services` IS
    `Art 2(5) the Regulation affects the application of the provision on the liability of providers of intermediary services` `the date asked` `the provision is a provision on the liability of providers of intermediary services in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065`


§ `Article 2(6): AI systems and models developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`
-- Only if the AI system or model was developed and put into service for that purpose alone.

-- src:48 | 6. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development.
@ref Art 2(6) (src:48)
-- The seat assumes the thing asked about is an AI system (the keel's first fact is passed as TRUE); whether software is an AI system is asked under Article 3(1).
@export Under Article 2(6), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system was specifically developed and put into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the AI system specifically developed and put into service?
      `the AI system was so developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the AI system developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development? Answer no if it serves any other purpose too.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(6), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` IS
    `Art 2(6) the Regulation applies to the AI system or model developed for the sole purpose of scientific research and development` `the date asked` TRUE `the AI system was specifically developed and put into service` `the AI system was so developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development`


§ `Article 2(7): personal data law (the Omnibus changed the provisions reserved)`
-- Only if personal data is processed in connection with the Regulation, or you ask whether the Regulation affects the data protection instruments.

-- src:50 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Without prejudice to Articles 4a and 59 of this Regulation, this Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. This Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680, without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59 of this Regulation.
@ref Art 2(7) first sentence (src:50) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427)
@export Under Article 2(7), as a deployer of an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to the personal data I process?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `personal data is processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in the Regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(7), as a deployer of an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to the personal data I process` IS
    `Art 2(7) Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to the personal data` `the date asked` `personal data is processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation`

-- src:50 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. Without prejudice to Articles 4a and 59 of this Regulation, this Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427 | 7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. This Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680, without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59 of this Regulation.
@ref Art 2(7) second sentence (src:50) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:427)
-- The date asked selects the text: the provisions reserved by "without prejudice" are Articles 10(5) and 59 as enacted, and Articles 4a and 59 as amended.
@export Under Article 2(7), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the instrument is Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, Directive 2002/58/EC or Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument you ask about Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, Directive 2002/58/EC or Directive (EU) 2016/680?
      `the number of the Article I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which Article of the Regulation do you ask about? Give its number, for example 9 for Article 9.
      `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any` IS A STRING @desc If the Article has a letter after its number, give it, for example a for Article 60a. Otherwise leave this empty.
      `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article` IS A NUMBER @desc Which paragraph of that Article do you ask about? Give its number, or 0 if you mean the whole Article.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(7), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` IS
    `Art 2(7) the Regulation affects the data protection instrument through the provision` `the date asked` `the instrument is Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, Directive 2002/58/EC or Directive (EU) 2016/680` `the provision I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the provision I ask about` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
            number IS `the number of the Article I ask about`
            letter IS `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any`
            paragraph IS `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article`


§ `Article 2(10): deployers who are natural persons in a purely personal non-professional activity`
-- Only if the deployer is a natural person using an AI system for a purely personal, non-professional activity.

-- src:54 | 10. This Regulation does not apply to obligations of deployers who are natural persons using AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity.
@ref Art 2(10) (src:54)
-- The seat assumes the deployer role (the person asking holds it), so only the two facts that the paragraph adds are asked.
@export Under Article 2(10), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to my obligations as a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a natural person?
      `I use AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(10), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to my obligations as a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` IS
    `Art 2(10) the Regulation applies to the obligations of the natural person deployer using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` `the date asked` `I am a natural person` `I use AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity`


§ `Article 2(12): AI systems released under free and open-source licences`
-- Only if the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence.

-- src:56 | 12. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems released under free and open-source licences, unless they are placed on the market or put into service as high-risk AI systems or as an AI system that falls under Article 5 or 50.
@ref Art 2(12) (src:56)
-- The system is "placed on the market or put into service as a high-risk AI system" when its route is Article 6(1) with Annex I or Article 6(2) with Annex III (the keel's seam S1: high-risk if and only if the route is not `Route neither`).
-- Whether the system falls under Article 5 or Article 50 is decided in other provisions of the Regulation; here it is a yes/no fact.
@export Under Article 2(12), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system released under a free and open-source licence?
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the AI system falls under Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system fall under Article 5 (prohibited AI practices)?
      `the AI system falls under Article 50` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system fall under Article 50 (transparency obligations for certain AI systems)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(12), as a deployer of an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` IS
    `Art 2(12) the Regulation applies to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` `the date asked` `the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence` (NOT (`the route by which the AI system is high-risk` EQUALS `Route neither`)) `the AI system falls under Article 5` `the AI system falls under Article 50`


§ `Article 3(1): is it an AI system?`
-- A definition: no date is asked, because Article 3 applies with the provision that uses it.

-- src:66 | (1) ‘AI system’ means a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy and that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment, and that, for explicit or implicit objectives, infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions that can influence physical or virtual environments;
@ref Art 3(1) (src:66)
-- "that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment" says what a system may do; it is not a fact asked (fork F-3-1 of the keel).
@export Under Article 3(1), as a deployer of an AI system, is the software I use an AI system?
GIVEN `the system is machine-based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the system machine-based?
      `the system is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the system designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy?
      `for explicit or implicit objectives, the system infers from the input it receives how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations or decisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the system, for explicit or implicit objectives, infer from the input it receives how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations or decisions?
      `those outputs can influence physical or virtual environments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can those outputs influence physical or virtual environments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(1), as a deployer of an AI system, is the software I use an AI system` IS
    `Art 3(1) the system is an AI system` `the system is machine-based` `the system is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy` `for explicit or implicit objectives, the system infers from the input it receives how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations or decisions` `those outputs can influence physical or virtual environments`


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`
-- The role question of the seat: the other questions of this file assume the answer is yes.

-- src:69 | (4) ‘deployer’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body using an AI system under its authority except where the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity;
@ref Art 3(4) (src:69)
-- The role question of this seat.
@export Under Article 3(4), as a deployer of an AI system, does the definition of a deployer fit me?
GIVEN `I use the AI system under my authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the AI system under your authority?
      `I use the AI system in the course of a personal non-professional activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use the AI system in the course of a personal non-professional activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(4), as a deployer of an AI system, does the definition of a deployer fit me` IS
    `Art 3(4) the party is a deployer` `I use the AI system under my authority` `I use the AI system in the course of a personal non-professional activity`

-- src:73 | (8) ‘operator’ means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor;
@ref Art 3(8) (src:73)
-- No fact is asked: the seat fixes the role passed to the keel (a person who holds another role asks that seat's question).
@export Under Article 3(8), as a deployer of an AI system, am I an operator?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(8), as a deployer of an AI system, am I an operator` IS
    `Art 3(8) the role is an operator` Deployer


§ `Article 3(14), (14a), (14b): safety component, SME, small mid-cap enterprise (the Omnibus replaced one and inserted two)`
-- The date asked selects the text: (14) was replaced on 27 July 2026, and (14a) and (14b) exist only from then.

-- src:82 | (14a) ‘micro, small and medium-sized enterprise’ or ‘SME’ means a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC;
@ref Art 3(14a) (src:82)
-- Whether the enterprise is one "as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC" is decided in that Recommendation: a yes/no fact here.
@export Under Article 3(14a), as a deployer of an AI system, am I a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your enterprise a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(14a), as a deployer of an AI system, am I a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise` IS
    `Art 3(14a) the enterprise is a micro, small and medium-sized enterprise` `the date asked` `my enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC`

-- src:83 | (14b) ‘small mid-cap enterprise’ or ‘SMC’ means a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099;
@ref Art 3(14b) (src:83)
-- Whether the enterprise is one "as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099" is decided in that Recommendation: a yes/no fact here.
@export Under Article 3(14b), as a deployer of an AI system, am I a small mid-cap enterprise?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your enterprise a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Commission Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(14b), as a deployer of an AI system, am I a small mid-cap enterprise` IS
    `Art 3(14b) the enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise` `the date asked` `my enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099`


§ `Article 3(23): substantial modification`
-- Only if a change has been made to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service.

-- src:93 | (23) ‘substantial modification’ means a change to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service which is not foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider and as a result of which the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected or results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed;
@ref Art 3(23) (src:93)
@export Under Article 3(23), as a deployer of an AI system, is the change a substantial modification?
GIVEN `the change is to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change made to the AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service?
      `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the change foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider?
      `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of the change, is the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 affected?
      `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the change result in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(23), as a deployer of an AI system, is the change a substantial modification` IS
    `Art 3(23) the change is a substantial modification` `the change is to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service` `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider` `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed`


§ `Article 3(49): serious incident`
-- Only if something has gone wrong with an AI system.

-- src:121 | (49) ‘serious incident’ means an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system that directly or indirectly leads to any of the following:
-- src:122 | (a) the death of a person, or serious harm to a person’s health;
-- src:123 | (b) a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure;
-- src:124 | (c) the infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights;
-- src:125 | (d) serious harm to property or the environment;
@ref Art 3(49) (src:121-125)
@export Under Article 3(49), as a deployer of an AI system, is the event a serious incident?
GIVEN `the event is an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the event an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system?
      `it directly or indirectly leads to the death of a person, or serious harm to a person's health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it directly or indirectly lead to the death of a person, or serious harm to a person's health?
      `it directly or indirectly leads to a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it directly or indirectly lead to a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure?
      `it directly or indirectly leads to the infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it directly or indirectly lead to the infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights?
      `it directly or indirectly leads to serious harm to property or the environment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it directly or indirectly lead to serious harm to property or the environment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(49), as a deployer of an AI system, is the event a serious incident` IS
    `Art 3(49) the event is a serious incident` `the event is an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system` `it directly or indirectly leads to the death of a person, or serious harm to a person's health` `it directly or indirectly leads to a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure` `it directly or indirectly leads to the infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights` `it directly or indirectly leads to serious harm to property or the environment`


§ `Article 4: AI literacy (the Omnibus replaced Article 4)`
-- Article 4 applies from 2 February 2025 (Chapter I). The date asked selects the text: ensure a sufficient level (as enacted) or support the development (from 27 July 2026).

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596 | Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596)
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it, so the keel's role fact is passed as TRUE. Whether the definition of the role fits is asked once, in the question under Article 3.
@export Under Article 4(1), as a deployer of an AI system, do I owe the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(1), as a deployer of an AI system, do I owe the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` IS
    `Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` `the date asked` FALSE TRUE

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596 | Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596)
-- The judgments ("sufficient", "support the development") are yes/no facts here: the person decides them.
@export Under Article 4(1), as a deployer of an AI system, do my measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `my measures concern the AI literacy of my staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures concern the AI literacy of your staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on your behalf?
      `my measures take into account the technical knowledge, experience, education and training of those persons and the context the AI systems are to be used in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures take into account the technical knowledge, experience, education and training of those persons and the context the AI systems are to be used in?
      `my measures consider the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your measures consider the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used?
      `my measures are to ensure, to my best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your measures to ensure, to your best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy? (Only the Regulation as it stood before 27 July 2026 reads this answer.)
      `my measures are to support the development of AI literacy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your measures to support the development of AI literacy? (Only the Regulation from 27 July 2026 reads this answer.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(1), as a deployer of an AI system, do my measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` IS
    `Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` `the date asked` `my measures concern the AI literacy of my staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on my behalf` `my measures take into account the technical knowledge, experience, education and training of those persons and the context the AI systems are to be used in` `my measures consider the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used` `my measures are to ensure, to my best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy` `my measures are to support the development of AI literacy`

