§ `Under Annex II: the offences for the use exception`

§§ `Annex II`

@export Under Annex II point 1 to 16, as a deployer of an AI system, is the offence for which I use the system one of the criminal offences listed in Annex II?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Annex II offence` @desc Which of the offences listed in Annex II is it? Choose the entry that names the offence, or the choice for no listed offence.
      `the criminal organisation is involved in one or more of the offences listed above` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offence is participation in a criminal organisation: is the organisation involved in one or more of the other offences listed in Annex II?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Annex II point 1 to 16, as a deployer of an AI system, is the offence for which I use the system one of the criminal offences listed in Annex II` IS
    `Annex II the offence is listed` `the offence` `the criminal organisation is involved in one or more of the offences listed above`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat deployer from part P2 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P2-seat-deployer.l4: the seat of a deployer of an AI system, over the layer-1 modules of part P2 (Article 4a, Articles 8 to 15, Annex IV).
-- It calls the layer-1 rules and never restates one. Every question has @export and @desc and takes plain inputs; the records a rule expects are built in a WHERE.
-- The shared inputs have the same names and @desc in every question: the date asked; the route by which the AI system is high-risk; the date it was placed on the market or put into service; whether its design was significantly changed since Chapter III applied.
-- A result of NOTHING is "not covered" (not yet applicable, saved by Article 111(2), or outside what the text says); JUST FALSE is the text's own "no".
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it (the role question below calls the keel's definition once).

§ `The role and the applicability of the provisions`

@export Under Article 4a, as a deployer of an AI system, am I a deployer within the meaning of Article 3(4)?
GIVEN `the party uses an AI system under its authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use an AI system under your authority?
      `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system used in the course of a personal non-professional activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a, as a deployer of an AI system, am I a deployer within the meaning of Article 3(4)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(4) the party is a deployer` `the party uses an AI system under its authority` `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity`)

@export Under Article 4a, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

@export Under Article 8, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8, as a deployer of an AI system, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)


§ `Under Article 4a: processing special categories of personal data for bias detection and correction`

@export Under Article 4a(2), as a deployer of an AI system, may I exceptionally process special categories of personal data to ensure bias detection and correction?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, genetic or biometric data, health, sex life or sexual orientation)?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725?
      `such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations?
      `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place?
      `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with?
      `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data?
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation?
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations?
      `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties?
      `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first?
      `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the processing you have in mind: is it the case that the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a(2), as a deployer of an AI system, may I exceptionally process special categories of personal data to ensure bias detection and correction` IS
    `Art 4a(2) the provider or deployer may exceptionally process special categories of personal data` `the date asked` FALSE (`the route by which the AI system is high-risk` EQUALS `Route neither`) (NOT (`the route by which the AI system is high-risk` EQUALS `Route neither`)) (`Art 3(37) the category is a special category of personal data` `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725`) `such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data`

