-- P5-seat-deployer: the questions a deployer of an AI system can ask of Articles 46 and 49 and Annex VIII Section C. A seat module calls layer 1 and restates no rule.

§ `Article 40: does the group apply?`

-- The applicability question: Article 113 as amended dates Chapter III Section 5 (Articles 40 to 49) and the Annexes of this part by its second paragraph (the General group; keel fork F-113-groups, assumed).
@export Under Article 40, as a deployer of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 40, as a deployer of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

§ `Under Article 46(2)`

-- May I put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation? (layer 1: Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk A...)
@export Under Article 46(2), as a deployer of an AI system, may I put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? It matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I: Article 2(2) then limits which provisions of the Regulation apply to it. Answer no if it is not, or if you do not know.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Under Article 2(2) this matters only for Articles 57 to 59, so it does not change the answer to this question. Answer no if you do not know.
      `the deployer is a law-enforcement authority or a civil protection authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the deployer is a law-enforcement authority or a civil protection authority? Answer yes or no.
      `the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency for exceptional reasons of public security, or a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency for exceptional reasons of public security, or a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons? Answer yes or no.
      `the authorisation referred to in paragraph 1 is requested during or after the use without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this so: the authorisation referred to in paragraph 1 is requested during or after the use without undue delay? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 46(2), as a deployer of an AI system, may I put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` IS
    `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the deployer is a law-enforcement authority or a civil protection authority` `the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency for exceptional reasons of public security, or a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons` `the authorisation referred to in paragraph 1 is requested during or after the use without undue delay`

