-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat deployer from part P7 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P7-seat-deployer: THE SEAT LAYER for a deployer of an AI system, over the layer-1 modules of Articles 57 to 71 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: the deployer. In this part a deployer appears as a participant in a provider's testing in real world conditions (Article 60(4)(h), (j)), as the entity that enters Section C data
-- into the EU database when it is a public authority (Article 71(3)), as a recipient of the Member State's awareness raising and training (Article 62(1)(b), (c)), and as an addressee
-- of the national competent authorities' guidance and advice (Article 70(8)). Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 function.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number, each with an @desc. The date asked comes first. `General` (Chapter VI and Chapter VIII) applies from 2 August 2026;
-- the group of Chapter VII from 2 August 2025. Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled).
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Under Article 57: the group General and the role`

-- The applicability question for the provision group `General` that Article 57 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 57, as a deployer of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a deployer of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- The role question. Article 3(4) defines the deployer: whoever uses an AI system under its authority, except in the course of a personal non-professional activity. The other questions of this seat assume you hold this role.
@export Under Article 57, as a deployer of an AI system, am I a deployer of an AI system?
GIVEN `the party uses an AI system under its authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use an AI system under your authority?
      `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system used in the course of a personal non-professional activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a deployer of an AI system, am I a deployer of an AI system` IS
    `Art 3(4) the party is a deployer` `the party uses an AI system under its authority` `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity`


§ `Under Article 60: testing in real world conditions in which a deployer takes part`

-- These questions arise only if a provider organises testing of an AI system in real world conditions in cooperation with you.

-- Article 60(4)(h).
@export Under Article 60, as a deployer of an AI system, if a provider organises the testing in cooperation with me, have I been informed of all relevant aspects and given the instructions for use, and have we concluded an agreement on roles and responsibilities?
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers? Answer yes or no.
      `the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate? Answer yes or no.
      `the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13? Answer yes or no.
      `the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a deployer of an AI system, if a provider organises the testing in cooperation with me, have I been informed of all relevant aspects and given the instructions for use, and have we concluded an agreement on roles and responsibilities` IS
    `Art 60(4)(h) the deployers taking part have been informed and an agreement concluded` `the provider or prospective provider organises the testing in cooperation with one or more deployers or prospective deployers` `the deployers or prospective deployers have been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to their decision to participate` `the deployers or prospective deployers have been given the relevant instructions for use of the AI system referred to in Article 13` `the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer have concluded an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities`

-- Article 60(4)(j): by the provider or prospective provider, as well as by the deployers or prospective deployers through persons suitably qualified in the relevant field with the necessary capacity, training and authority.
@export Under Article 60, as a deployer of an AI system, is the testing effectively overseen as the Regulation requires, by the provider and by the deployers through suitably qualified persons?
GIVEN `the testing is effectively overseen by the provider or prospective provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing is effectively overseen by the provider or prospective provider? Answer yes or no.
      `deployers or prospective deployers take part in the testing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that deployers or prospective deployers take part in the testing? Answer yes or no.
      `the testing is effectively overseen by the deployers or prospective deployers through persons who are suitably qualified in the relevant field and have the necessary capacity, training and authority to perform their tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing is effectively overseen by the deployers or prospective deployers through persons who are suitably qualified in the relevant field and have the necessary capacity, training and authority to perform their tasks? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a deployer of an AI system, is the testing effectively overseen as the Regulation requires, by the provider and by the deployers through suitably qualified persons` IS
    `Art 60(4)(j) the testing is effectively overseen` `the testing is effectively overseen by the provider or prospective provider` `deployers or prospective deployers take part in the testing` `the testing is effectively overseen by the deployers or prospective deployers through persons who are suitably qualified in the relevant field and have the necessary capacity, training and authority to perform their tasks`


§ `Under Article 62: awareness raising and training`

-- These questions arise only if you are a deployer in a Member State that undertakes the actions of Article 62(1).

-- Article 62(1)(b).
@export Under Article 62, as a deployer of an AI system, has my Member State organised specific awareness raising and training activities on the Regulation tailored to the needs of deployers?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the Member State organises specific awareness raising activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups and deployers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Member State organises specific awareness raising activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups and deployers? Answer yes or no.
      `the Member State organises specific training activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups and deployers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Member State organises specific training activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups and deployers? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 62, as a deployer of an AI system, has my Member State organised specific awareness raising and training activities on the Regulation tailored to the needs of deployers` IS
    `Art 62(1)(b) the Member State has organised specific awareness raising and training activities tailored to the needs of SMEs and deployers` `the date asked` `the Member State organises specific awareness raising activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups and deployers` `the Member State organises specific training activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups and deployers`

-- Article 62(1)(c).
@export Under Article 62, as a deployer of an AI system, has my Member State used the existing dedicated channels to give me advice and respond to my queries about the implementation of the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the Member State utilises the existing dedicated channels for communication with SMEs including start-ups, deployers and other innovators to provide advice and respond to queries about the implementation of this Regulation, including as regards participation in AI regulatory sandboxes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Member State utilises the existing dedicated channels for communication with SMEs including start-ups, deployers and other innovators to provide advice and respond to queries about the implementation of this Regulation, including as regards participation in AI regulatory sandboxes? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 62, as a deployer of an AI system, has my Member State used the existing dedicated channels to give me advice and respond to my queries about the implementation of the Regulation` IS
    `Art 62(1)(c) the Member State has utilised the existing dedicated channels to provide advice and respond to queries` `the date asked` `the Member State utilises the existing dedicated channels for communication with SMEs including start-ups, deployers and other innovators to provide advice and respond to queries about the implementation of this Regulation, including as regards participation in AI regulatory sandboxes`


§ `Under Article 64: the group of Chapter VII`

-- Chapter VII is mostly about officials. What it means to a deployer: the national competent authorities may give guidance and advice, in particular to SMEs and SMCs (Article 70(8)); the European Data Protection Supervisor supervises Union institutions (Article 70(9)).

-- The applicability question for the provision group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` that Article 64 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 64, as a deployer of an AI system, does Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 64, as a deployer of an AI system, does Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- Article 70(8), first sentence. As enacted: SMEs including start-ups. As amended (from 27 July 2026): SMEs, including start-ups, and small mid-cap enterprises (SMCs).
@export Under Article 70, as a deployer of an AI system, is my enterprise one to whom the national competent authorities direct guidance and advice on the implementation of the Regulation in particular?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your enterprise a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC?
      `the enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your enterprise a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 70, as a deployer of an AI system, is my enterprise one to whom the national competent authorities direct guidance and advice on the implementation of the Regulation in particular` IS
    `Art 70(8) the enterprise is one to whom guidance and advice are directed in particular` `the date asked` `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` `the enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099`

-- Article 70(9).
@export Under Article 70, as a deployer of an AI system, if I am a Union institution, body, office or agency within the scope of the Regulation, does the European Data Protection Supervisor act as the competent authority for my supervision?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation? Answer yes or no.
      `the European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the competent authority for their supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the competent authority for their supervision? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 70, as a deployer of an AI system, if I am a Union institution, body, office or agency within the scope of the Regulation, does the European Data Protection Supervisor act as the competent authority for my supervision` IS
    `Art 70(9) the European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the competent authority for the supervision of Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies` `the date asked` `Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation` `the European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the competent authority for their supervision`


§ `Under Article 71: the EU database`

