§ `Article 78: Confidentiality`
-- Arises only for the confidentiality of information obtained in the application of the Regulation; the provider question arises only if the provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority.

-- Calls `Art 78(3) first sentence the disclosure of the information without prior consultation is barred`.
@export Under Article 78(3), as a deployer of an AI system, is the disclosure of the information exchanged on a confidential basis barred without prior consultation of me as the deployer?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission?
      `the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities?
      `the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests?
      `the originating national competent authority and the deployer have been consulted before the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating national competent authority and the deployer have been consulted before the disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 78(3), as a deployer of an AI system, is the disclosure of the information exchanged on a confidential basis barred without prior consultation of me as the deployer` IS
    `Art 78(3) first sentence the disclosure of the information without prior consultation is barred` `the date asked` `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission` `the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities` `the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests` `the originating national competent authority and the deployer have been consulted before the disclosure`

§ `Article 79: Procedure at national level for dealing with AI systems presenting a risk`
-- Arises only if a market surveillance authority has found that an AI system presents a risk.

-- Calls `Art 79(2) fourth sentence the relevant operators must cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies`.
@export Under Article 79(2), as a deployer of an AI system, must I, as a relevant operator, cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the market surveillance authority is carrying out an evaluation under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the market surveillance authority is carrying out an evaluation under this paragraph?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 79(2), as a deployer of an AI system, must I, as a relevant operator, cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies` IS
    `Art 79(2) fourth sentence the relevant operators must cooperate as necessary with the market surveillance authority and with the other national public authorities or bodies` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the market surveillance authority is carrying out an evaluation under this paragraph`

-- Calls `Art 79(2) second subparagraph the market surveillance authority must without undue delay require the relevant operator to take all appropriate corrective actions`.
@export Under Article 79(2), as a deployer of an AI system, must the market surveillance authority without undue delay require me to take all appropriate corrective actions?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the market surveillance authority, or the market surveillance authority in cooperation with the national public authority referred to in Article 77(1), finds in the course of the evaluation that the AI system does not comply with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the market surveillance authority, or the market surveillance authority in cooperation with the national public authority referred to in Article 77(1), finds in the course of the evaluation that the AI system does not comply with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 79(2), as a deployer of an AI system, must the market surveillance authority without undue delay require me to take all appropriate corrective actions` IS
    `Art 79(2) second subparagraph the market surveillance authority must without undue delay require the relevant operator to take all appropriate corrective actions` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the market surveillance authority, or the market surveillance authority in cooperation with the national public authority referred to in Article 77(1), finds in the course of the evaluation that the AI system does not comply with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation`

-- Calls `Art 79(2) second subparagraph the number of days within which the operator must take the corrective action`.
@export Under Article 79(2), as a deployer of an AI system, within how many days must I take the corrective action?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the number of days that the 15 working days cover` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days that the 15 working days cover? Give a number.
      `there is a figure for the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a figure for this: the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides? Answer no if there is none.
      `the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides? Give a number (any number if you answered no to the question before).
      `there is a figure for the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a figure for this: the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes? Answer no if there is none.
      `the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes? Give a number (any number if you answered no to the question before).
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 79(2), as a deployer of an AI system, within how many days must I take the corrective action` IS
    `Art 79(2) second subparagraph the number of days within which the operator must take the corrective action` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the number of days that the 15 working days cover` `the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides, if there is one` `the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes, if there is one`
    WHERE
        `the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides, if there is one` MEANS IF `there is a figure for the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides` THEN JUST `the number of days that the relevant Union harmonisation legislation provides` ELSE NOTHING
        `the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes, if there is one` MEANS IF `there is a figure for the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes` THEN JUST `the number of days that the market surveillance authority prescribes` ELSE NOTHING

-- Calls `Art 79(4) the operator must ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that it has made available on the Union market`.
@export Under Article 79(4), as a deployer of an AI system, must I ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all my AI systems made available on the Union market?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI systems concerned are AI systems that the operator has made available on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI systems concerned are AI systems that you have made available on the Union market?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 79(4), as a deployer of an AI system, must I ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all my AI systems made available on the Union market` IS
    `Art 79(4) the operator must ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that it has made available on the Union market` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the AI systems concerned are AI systems that the operator has made available on the Union market`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat deployer from part P9 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 -- P9 -- THE SEAT LAYER, Articles 80 to 112.
--
-- SEAT: a deployer of an AI system.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions this person would ask
-- about the Articles of P9 (market surveillance of AI systems, complaints and explanations, enforcement of the rules on
-- general-purpose AI models, codes of conduct and guidelines, penalties, and the final provisions). Nothing here is new law:
-- each question calls one layer-1 function and builds the record that function expects (the `AI system`) in a WHERE from
-- the answers. The rules a question calls are the ones that carry the quotes, the glosses and the NOTHING/FALSE branches.
-- Every question except the role question takes `the date asked`, so the answer is the Regulation as it stood or will stand on that date; a question
-- about an AI system also takes the AI system's route, the date it was placed on the market and whether its design has been
-- significantly changed, for Article 111(2). A group that is not yet in application answers NOTHING, never JUST FALSE.
-- The applicability question of each group the seat meets is the first question of its group of Articles.
-- The seat's own role is asked once, in the role question, which calls the keel's definition and has no date (a definition
-- of Article 3 is not asked on a date here); the other questions assume it.
-- Powers and duties of an official (the Commission, the AI Office, a market surveillance authority, the European Data
-- Protection Supervisor, a Member State) appear only as what they mean to this seat.
§ `Under Article 80: the applicability question for the group General`

@ref Art 113
@export Under Article 80, as a deployer of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 80, as a deployer of an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

§ `The seat's role: Article 3(4)`

@ref Art 3
@export Under Article 80, as a deployer of an AI system, am I a deployer within the meaning of Article 3(4)?
GIVEN `the party uses an AI system under its authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you use an AI system under your authority?
      `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system used in the course of a personal non-professional activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 80, as a deployer of an AI system, am I a deployer within the meaning of Article 3(4)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(4) the party is a deployer` `the party uses an AI system under its authority` `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity`)

§ `Under Article 82(1)`

@ref Art 82(1)
@export Under Article 82(1), as a deployer of an AI system, must the market surveillance authority require me, as the relevant operator, to take all appropriate measures?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I to the Regulation? Answer no if you do not know. This matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Answer no if you do not know. It decides nothing about the Articles asked here (it matters only to Articles 57, 58 and 59), but the same question is asked of every provision that Article 2(2) can cut off.
      `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk?
      `the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)?
      `the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation?
      `the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 82(1), as a deployer of an AI system, must the market surveillance authority require me, as the relevant operator, to take all appropriate measures` IS
    `Art 82(1) the market surveillance authority must require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the market surveillance authority has found under Article 79 that the AI system presents a risk` `the market surveillance authority has consulted the relevant national public authority referred to in Article 77(1)` `the high-risk AI system complies with this Regulation` `the AI system presents a risk to the health or safety of persons, to fundamental rights, or to other aspects of public interest protection`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

§ `Under Article 82(2)`

@ref Art 82(2)
@export Under Article 82(2), as a deployer of an AI system, have I, as the relevant operator, ensured that corrective action is taken?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I to the Regulation? Answer no if you do not know. This matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Answer no if you do not know. It decides nothing about the Articles asked here (it matters only to Articles 57, 58 and 59), but the same question is asked of every provision that Article 2(2) can cut off.
      `the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)?
      `the number of the AI systems concerned that the operator has made available on the Union market` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the AI systems concerned has the operator made available on the Union market?
      `the number of those AI systems in respect of which corrective action has been taken within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority` IS A NUMBER @desc In respect of how many of those AI systems has corrective action been taken within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 82(2), as a deployer of an AI system, have I, as the relevant operator, ensured that corrective action is taken` IS
    `Art 82(2) the provider or other relevant operator has ensured that corrective action is taken` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the market surveillance authority has required the operator to take measures under Article 82(1)` `the number of the AI systems concerned that the operator has made available on the Union market` `the number of those AI systems in respect of which corrective action has been taken within the timeline prescribed by the market surveillance authority`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

§ `Under Article 86(1)`

